<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The EA-6B Prowler's service-life upgrades (owner, 22 Nov 2026: "full, with ICAP upgrades"; docs/development/ea6b-prowler.md). Fittings
    of ours, beside the Prowler's own upgrade tree, never in it. The jet starts as the ICAP of 1976; both go on its fin-top receivers (D'thorga
    Patches' part) or, without them, its jammer pods, so one replaces the other. Each widens its jamming field through D'thorga Patches' hook on
    the Prowler's own radius. The factors are authored: no source gives the real gain in a form a radius can follow. Materials, work and skill
    are authored too. Not yet tested in game.
  -->

  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
    <!-- ICAP II, first delivered 1982 (secondary: the Congressional Research Service's report RL30639, 2001; Wikipedia gives 1980 for its first
         flight): upgraded receivers, displays and software, jamming in two frequency bands at once, with its Block 82 to 89A updates, the last
         of which (initial operating capability about 2000, secondary: FAS) brought satellite navigation with an inertial set (Litton ASN-172,
         secondary: FAS). Here: the field 10 % wider (authored) and full navigation. -->
    <defName>PhobosFitting_ProwlerIcapII</defName>
    <iconPath>Phobos/Vehicles/Fittings/ProwlerIcapII</iconPath>
    <label>ICAP II suite</label>
    <description>The Prowler's second improved suite, in service from 1982 and updated through the 1990s: better receivers and software that jam two bands at once, and in its last form satellite navigation. While it has power, its jamming field reaches about a tenth further, and it keeps its track between places in any weather.</description>
    <roles><li>EwReceivers</li></roles>
    <loadouts><li>PhobosVehicleLoadout_Prowler</li></loadouts>
    <materials><Steel>10</Steel><ComponentIndustrial>8</ComponentIndustrial><ComponentSpacer>1</ComponentSpacer></materials>
    <work>8000</work>
    <minSkill>8</minSkill>
    <researchPrerequisite>MicroelectronicsBasics</researchPrerequisite>
    <grants><li>ProwlerIcapII</li></grants>
    <jamRadiusFactor>1.10</jamRadiusFactor>
    <parameterFloors>
      <li><system>PhobosVehicleSystem_Avionics</system><parameter>navigationFull</parameter><value>1</value></li>
    </parameterFloors>
    <loads>
      <li>
        <name>prowlerIcapII</name>
        <label>ICAP II suite</label>
        <description>The ICAP II receivers and computer.</description>
        <amps>6</amps>
        <shedOrder>4</shedOrder>
      </li>
    </loads>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>

  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>
    <!-- ICAP III: contract March 1998, first flight 16 Nov 2001 (secondary: CRS RL30639; the US Navy's fact file), first deployed 2005 with VAQ-139
         and first in combat in February 2006 (primary: VAQ-139's history, airpac.navy.mil). The ALQ-218 receiver for selective-reactive
         jamming, which jams only the emitters it hears, and the USQ-113 communications jammer. Here: the field 25 % wider (authored), full
         navigation and a warning receiver. The communications jammer is not modelled (our radio work is set aside). -->
    <defName>PhobosFitting_ProwlerIcapIII</defName>
    <iconPath>Phobos/Vehicles/Fittings/ProwlerIcapIII</iconPath>
    <label>ICAP III suite</label>
    <description>The Prowler's last suite, first deployed in 2005: a receiver that hears each enemy emitter and jams only those it hears, with a radio jammer beside it. While it has power, its jamming field reaches about a quarter further, it navigates by satellite, and it always knows when a radar has it.</description>
    <roles><li>EwReceivers</li></roles>
    <loadouts><li>PhobosVehicleLoadout_Prowler</li></loadouts>
    <materials><Steel>10</Steel><ComponentIndustrial>6</ComponentIndustrial><ComponentSpacer>3</ComponentSpacer></materials>
    <work>12000</work>
    <minSkill>10</minSkill>
    <researchPrerequisite>AdvancedFabrication</researchPrerequisite>
    <grants><li>ProwlerIcapIII</li></grants>
    <jamRadiusFactor>1.25</jamRadiusFactor>
    <parameterFloors>
      <li><system>PhobosVehicleSystem_Avionics</system><parameter>navigationFull</parameter><value>1</value></li>
      <li><system>PhobosVehicleSystem_Avionics</system><parameter>warning</parameter><value>1</value></li>
    </parameterFloors>
    <loads>
      <li>
        <name>prowlerIcapIII</name>
        <label>ICAP III suite</label>
        <description>The ICAP III receiver, jammer controls and computers.</description>
        <amps>8</amps>
        <shedOrder>4</shedOrder>
      </li>
    </loads>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFittingDef>

  <!-- Enemy sets: another faction's Prowler may arrive as a later version, as the real ones were refitted. Tech levels authored. -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFitSetDef>
    <defName>PhobosFitSet_ProwlerIcapII</defName>
    <minTech>Industrial</minTech>
    <maxTech>Spacer</maxTech>
    <fittings>
      <li>PhobosFitting_ProwlerIcapII</li>
    </fittings>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFitSetDef>

  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFitSetDef>
    <defName>PhobosFitSet_ProwlerIcapIII</defName>
    <minTech>Spacer</minTech>
    <maxTech>Archotech</maxTech>
    <fittings>
      <li>PhobosFitting_ProwlerIcapIII</li>
    </fittings>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleFitSetDef>
</Defs>
